    "verseCount": 6,
    "content": "<p class=\"p\"><span data-number=\"1\" data-sid=\"JOB 25:1\" class=\"v\">1</span>Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"2\" data-sid=\"JOB 25:2\" class=\"v\">2</span>“Dominion and fear are with him.</p><p data-vid=\"JOB 25:2\" class=\"q2\">He makes peace in his high places.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"3\" data-sid=\"JOB 25:3\" class=\"v\">3</span>Can his armies be counted?</p><p data-vid=\"JOB 25:3\" class=\"q2\">On whom does his light not arise?</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"4\" data-sid=\"JOB 25:4\" class=\"v\">4</span>How then can man be just with God?</p><p data-vid=\"JOB 25:4\" class=\"q2\">Or how can he who is born of a woman be clean?</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"5\" data-sid=\"JOB 25:5\" class=\"v\">5</span>Behold, even the moon has no brightness,</p><p data-vid=\"JOB 25:5\" class=\"q2\">and the stars are not pure in his sight;</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"6\" data-sid=\"JOB 25:6\" class=\"v\">6</span>How much less man, who is a worm,</p><p data-vid=\"JOB 25:6\" class=\"q2\">and the son of man, who is a worm!”</p>",
